        "code": {
          "text": "General appearance and interaction"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert, well appearing, speaking in full sentences, and in no acute distress."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Facial and anterior neck skin examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Forehead, nasal bridge, both malar areas, and anterior neck to upper chest involved. Forehead, nose, and neck are erythematous and warm, mildly tender, with sensation intact. Both upper cheeks have 2–3 cm healing areas where blisters ruptured; areas are pink and moist with no slough or pus. Skin is soft with no circumferential neck burn or tight eschar. No charring; minimal singeing of eyebrows and sideburns. No clinical cellulitis at present."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Estimated total body surface area involved"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 5–6% TBSA."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Skin pattern"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Clear T-shirt line and safety-glasses border pattern; documented as appearing consistent with a flash burn rather than prolonged contact or pure sunburn."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-17",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Eye examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No periorbital oedema; eyelids open fully; no burns at lid margins. Conjunctiva mildly injected with no chemosis. PERRLA and EOMI. Visual acuity grossly normal; able to read a poster. No photophobia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-18",
